🚽 Test case: a STDROT_ANY parameter (slorp's) must reject a numeric
🚽 array identifier. Variable stores an array's backing pointer and a
🚽 scalar's value in the same union (value.array_data aliases
🚽 value.ivalue), and ast_expr_to_stdrot_value()'s VAR_INT case reads
🚽 that union unconditionally with no is_array check -- without this
🚽 rejection, slorp's deprecated write-back path could overwrite the
🚽 array's backing pointer with whatever the user typed at stdin.
skibidi main {
    rizz arr[2] = {1, 2};
    slorp(arr);
    bussin 0;
}
